Shoalcade build fix for the Windows (MinGW GCC, CMake) libretro core. No effect on any other build.
The multi-ISA tiers picked MSVC's /arch:AVX and /arch:AVX2 for every WIN32 build, so GCC on Windows was handed
MSVC flags (26 compile failures). Test the compiler, not the OS: MSVC keeps /arch, MinGW GCC takes the GCC branch
(-msse4.1 -mavx ...), exactly as on Linux.

diff --git a/pcsx2/CMakeLists.txt b/pcsx2/CMakeLists.txt
index 6a1f82b..3d197b1 100644
--- a/pcsx2/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/pcsx2/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -572,7 +572,7 @@ if(DISABLE_ADVANCE_SIMD AND _M_X86)
 	if(USE_GCC)
 		target_link_options(PCSX2_FLAGS INTERFACE -Wno-odr)
 	endif()
-	if(WIN32)
+	if(MSVC)
 		set(compile_options_avx2 /arch:AVX2)
 		set(compile_options_avx  /arch:AVX)
 	elseif(USE_GCC)
